+            # ---- Prefetch I/O concurrency ----
+            #
+            # prefetch_io_workers controls how many prefetch *operations* (one
+            # per incoming request) can perform page-transfer I/O concurrently.
+            # This is a **per-rank** setting: each GPU rank runs its own
+            # HiCacheController with its own prefetch thread and I/O executor.
+            #
+            # Threading topology (per rank):
+            #
+            #   prefetch_thread  (1 thread — hit-query + dispatch)
+            #     └─ ThreadPoolExecutor "prefetch_io"  (prefetch_io_workers threads)
+            #          └─ _prefetch_io_task(operation)
+            #               └─ _page_transfer → batch_get_v1
+            #                    └─ CamaStorage._io_pool  (io_workers threads, default 16)
+            #                         └─ conn.get(key, sgl, size)  [shared RDMA conn]
+            #
+            # So the two pools are *nested*:
+            #   • prefetch_io_workers  — # of requests doing I/O in parallel
+            #   • io_workers (CAMA)    — # of keys fetched in parallel *within*
+            #                            a single batch_get_v1 call
+            #
+            # Peak concurrent RDMA ops ≈ prefetch_io_workers × io_workers, all
+            # funnelled through a single PriskvClient connection per rank (which
+            # is thread-safe but serialises at the transport level).
+            #
+            # Why the default is 2:
+            #   • The prefetch_thread itself is single-threaded and alternates
+            #     between hit-query (CPU + exists RPCs) and dispatching I/O.
+            #     With workers=1, hit-query and I/O are fully serial — the
+            #     thread blocks on _page_transfer before it can query the next
+            #     request.  workers=2 lets the next hit-query overlap with the
+            #     previous request's page transfer, roughly doubling throughput
+            #     when the prefetch queue is busy.
+            #   • Higher values (3–4) help only if the RDMA link or PrisKV
+            #     server can sustain the extra concurrency.  Because all workers
+            #     share one RDMA connection and one CamaStorage._io_pool, adding
+            #     more prefetch_io_workers mostly adds contention on the same
+            #     transport without improving bandwidth.
+            #   • The backup_thread (writes) is *not* affected — it runs in its
+            #     own thread and calls batch_set_v1 serially, sharing the same
+            #     CamaStorage._io_pool.  Raising prefetch_io_workers too high
+            #     can starve backup I/O of io_pool slots.
+            #
+            # To tune: monitor "prefetch_thread_func: shutdown complete" log for
+            # io_completed vs io_failed, and CAMA I/O stats for avg_latency.
+            # If avg_latency rises with more workers, the link is saturated.
+            self.prefetch_io_workers = int(
+                (storage_backend_extra_config or {}).get("prefetch_io_workers", 2)
+            )
